The ADOS domain calibrated severity scores were created to provide separate estimates of Social Affect (SA-CSS) and Restricted, Repetitive Behaviors (RRB-CSS) that are relatively independent of child characteristics (
Hus et al., 2014
). Using a sample of 2,509 probands with ASD from the Simons Simplex Collection (SSC), this study provides the first replication of the ADOS domain CSS in an independent sample. Consistent with the original standardization study, when applied to existing SSC data, the ADOS domain CSS were less influenced by age and cognitive ability compared to raw domain totals.
